# Git attributes — rules, not a commented-out template.
#
# The normalisation below is currently a no-op: all 38 tracked files are already
# LF. That is the point of writing it down now rather than after the first
# CRLF commit — `git add --renormalize .` produces an empty diff today, so this
# file can be added without a reformatting commit tangled up in it.

# Normalise everything to LF in the repository, whatever the working tree uses.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Be explicit for the formats this repository actually contains, so a new file
# type does not silently rely on `text=auto` guessing correctly.
*.tex   text
*.sty   text
*.cls   text
*.md    text
*.yml   text
*.yaml  text
*.html  text
*.json  text
*.gitignore text

# Binary: never line-ending-converted, never diffed as text. *.pdf is ignored
# today, but a deliberately versioned one must not be mangled — which is exactly
# the case the .gitignore rule would stop protecting the moment someone adds a
# `!keep-this.pdf` exception.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.otf   binary
*.ttf   binary
